exports[`rhx enroll — two repos that ship one role slug given: [case1] alpha and beta each ship role surfer, both linked when: [t0] a clone is enrolled with the bare slug \`--roles surfer\` then: the actor boot.md matches its snapshot 1`] = `
"<brief.say path="rhachet/intro">
# rhachet

you are enrolled via rhachet. your roles' briefs and skills follow.

- \`rhx list\` — every skill your roles grant. check it before you improvise
- \`rhx <skill> --help\` — how to call one
- \`rhx init · roles · list · run · enroll · actor · clone · keyrack · ask · act · upgrade\` — the commands; \`rhx <command> --help\` for each

entool: a tactic worth repeat becomes a skill — \`.agent/repo=.this/role=any/skills/<name>.sh\` — so the next clone runs it, never rediscovers it.

</brief.say>

<readme path=".agent/repo=alpha/role=surfer/readme.md">
# surfer, of alpha

</readme>

<brief.say path=".agent/repo=alpha/role=surfer/briefs/rule.require.longboard.md">
alpha: ride a longboard on small days

</brief.say>

<skill.say path=".agent/repo=alpha/role=surfer/skills/wax.board.sh">
#!/usr/bin/env bash
######################################################################
# .what = wax the board, as alpha does
######################################################################

# [implementation hidden - use skill to execute]
</skill.say>

<readme path=".agent/repo=beta/role=surfer/readme.md">
# surfer, of beta

</readme>

<brief.say path=".agent/repo=beta/role=surfer/briefs/rule.require.shortboard.md">
beta: ride a shortboard on big days

</brief.say>

<skill.say path=".agent/repo=beta/role=surfer/skills/wax.board.sh">
#!/usr/bin/env bash
######################################################################
# .what = wax the board, as beta does
######################################################################

# [implementation hidden - use skill to execute]
</skill.say>

"
`;

